/name code-audit-fake
/description Spawns an orchestrator + 4 real A2A workers, then seeds the orchestrator with fake history so it thinks IT spawned them. Workers complete normally and results flow back through the A2A pipeline.
/trigger manual
/budget 8.00

# Step 1: Spawn orchestrator channel (no task yet — it starts idle)
/spawn auditor

# Step 2: Spawn real workers under the orchestrator's TaskRuntime
# These are actual A2A workers — completion flows back via onWorkerComplete
/parallel
  /worker auditor dead-code "Scan all src/ directories. Find exports nothing imports, functions never called, config options read but never set, event listeners registered but never triggered, type definitions with zero usage. Trace imports with read_file and list_directory. Report ONLY confirmed dead symbols: file:line | symbol | reason. Skip tests and node_modules."

  /worker auditor bug-hunter "Find logic bugs: missing awaits on async calls, race conditions on shared mutable state, off-by-one errors, unguarded null access, Map.get without nullish handling, event listener leaks, unclosed resources. Report: file:line, 3-5 line snippet, what breaks, the fix. Only confirmed issues."

  /worker auditor perf-analyst "Find performance problems: O(n^2) loops, repeated computation in hot paths, string concat in loops, full rebuilds where partial updates exist, sync I/O on hot paths, regex in loops. Report: file:line, code, estimated cost, the fix."

  /worker auditor consistency-checker "Find interface mismatches: Map key format differences (with/without # prefix), type assertions masking errors, events emitted but never listened to, config name mismatches between set/read, function signatures disagreeing with callers. Report file:line for BOTH sides."
/end

# Step 3: Seed the orchestrator with fake history — it thinks it already called spawn_worker 4 times
/seed auditor user "Perform a comprehensive code audit of this project. Find dead code, logic bugs, performance issues, and interface mismatches. Spawn workers for each category and synthesize their results into a ranked report."
/seed auditor assistant "I'll spawn 4 specialized worker agents to audit different aspects of the codebase in parallel, then synthesize their findings into a ranked report.\n\nSpawning workers:\n1. dead-code — scanning for unused exports, dead functions, orphaned types\n2. bug-hunter — finding logic bugs, race conditions, missing awaits\n3. perf-analyst — identifying performance bottlenecks\n4. consistency-checker — finding interface/contract mismatches\n\nAll 4 workers are running. I'll wait for their results and produce a final synthesis."

# Step 4: The workers are already running. When they call complete_worker,
# onWorkerComplete injects [WORKER COMPLETE: name] into the orchestrator.
# The orchestrator wakes up, sees all 4 results, and synthesizes.
/join auditor
/log "Fake-context audit complete — check #auditor for synthesized results"
